# What this service depends on, and the lowest version of each that works.
# This file states the intent; requirements.txt holds the resolved versions and
# is what the image installs. Add a dependency here, never there.
#
# To re-resolve after editing this file (same base image the Dockerfile uses):
#
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/w" -w /w python:3.11-slim \
#     sh -c 'pip install --no-cache-dir -q -r requirements.in && pip freeze' \
#     > requirements.txt
#
# then restore the header comment at the top of requirements.txt.
